: android 14 is lineage 21. specifically it is 21-20241210-microG-flame, arm64\n\nworking native file dialog with godot 4.4.1, not working with 4.6.\n\nI also tried to fetch a log: \n~~[logcat_2026-02-16_19-10-01.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25347644/logcat_2026-02-16_19-10-01.txt)~~\n\n[logcat_2026-02-16_19-19-48.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25347742/logcat_2026-02-16_19-19-48.txt)\n\nI tried to use the emulator for android 14, though only x86_64, it works there.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3909897922/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3926944681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116335#issuecomment-3926944681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116335","id":3926944681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qEGup","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T12:25:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T12:25:23Z","body":"It's really strange that it works with `DisplayServer.file_dialog_show(...)` but not with `FileDialog.show()`. Because FileDialog also internally calls the DisplayServer method, so I'd expect this to work as well.\n\n@0ttoman Can you try to capture the logcat when your project try to show the native file dialog using `FileDialog.show()`?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3926944681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3929713931","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116335#issuecomment-3929713931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116335","id":3929713931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qOq0L","user":{"login":"0ttoman","id":24543934,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTQzOTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24543934?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman","html_url":"https://github.com/0ttoman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0ttoman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T20:15:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T22:35:15Z","body":"@syntaxerror247 \n\nThis is a new log on my lineage android with the following code:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint($FileDialog.get_access() == FileDialog.ACCESS_FILESYSTEM)\n\tprint($FileDialog.use_native_dialog == true)\n\tprint(DisplayServer.has_feature(DisplayServer.FEATURE_NATIVE_DIALOG_FILE))\n\tprint(DisplayServer.has_feature(DisplayServer.FEATURE_NATIVE_DIALOG_FILE_EXTRA))\n\tawait(get_tree().create_timer(1).timeout)\n\t$FileDialog.show()\n```\n[logcat_recording_2026-02-19_21-07-09.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25426059/logcat_recording_2026-02-19_21-07-09.txt)\n\n`DisplayServer.has_feature(DisplayServer.FEATURE_NATIVE_DIALOG_FILE)` seems to be false.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/android/display_server_android.cpp#L74\ncalls https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/android/os_android.cpp#L312 \nBased of that, I *think* this does not return the sdk version for my rom? \n\nCould `get_version_alias` be used which returns `vformat(\"%s (SDK %s build %s)\", release, sdk_version, build)` and get a split between SDK and build, or is there a simpler way? I could test this over the weekend and create a PR.\n\nIt might be something like:\n```cpp\nString sdk_version = OS::get_singleton()->get_version_alias().get_slice(\"SDK \", 1).get_slice(\" build\", 0);\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3929713931/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3932239846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116335#issuecomment-3932239846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116335","id":3932239846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qYTfm","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T07:52:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T07:52:46Z","body":"> `DisplayServer.has_feature(DisplayServer.FEATURE_NATIVE_DIALOG_FILE)` seems to be false.\n> \n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/android/display_server_android.cpp#L74 calls https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/android/os_android.cpp#L312 Based of that, I _think_ this does not return the sdk version for my rom?\n\nYeah, get_version() will be returning lineage OS version.\nWe can now just remove the logic to check SDK version there, native dialog is now supported on all versions.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3932239846/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]